diff --git a/help/settings/connections.md b/help/settings/connections.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8dc1247
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/settings/connections.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+---
+id: settings/connections
+title: Connections
+parent: settings
+summary: Choose which connection supplies each part of the till, check them, and go back to the current setup.
+tags: [connections, Alloys, Shopify, Zeller, iCloud, catalogue, orders, shared state, setup]
+related: [settings, settings/shopify, settings/cloud-sync, settings/hardware]
+updated: 2026-11-20
+roles: [manager, owner]
+---
+Open **More ▸ Settings ▸ Connections** to see where each part of the till gets its data, such as the catalogue, orders, stock, gift cards and the card reader.
+
+## Basic
+
+### What the screen shows
+Each part of the till has a row. The chips under it are the connections that can do that part, plus **Off** for the parts that are optional. A part marked *needed* (Catalogue, Orders and Shared state) cannot be switched off.
+
+The screen opens on what the till is doing today, so looking at it changes nothing. Nothing is saved until you tap **Save choice**, and saving never moves or deletes any data. Anything already held in an older service stays there.
+
+### Check connections
+Tap **Check connections** to ask every connection in use whether it is signed in and what it is missing. A part the login has no permission for shows a warning naming the permission to add.
+
+### Go back
+Once a choice is saved, **Go back to the current setup** removes it, and the till reads its setup the way it did before.
+
+## Deep
+
+### Warnings
+A needed part with nothing chosen blocks **Save choice**. An optional part that is off shows what the shop loses, for example that stock screens are hidden. A missing permission warns but does not block, because the rest of the till still works.
+
+## Advanced
+
+| Job | Where |
+|---|---|
+| The screen | `Connections` in `src/screens/Connections.tsx` |
+| Rows, warnings and the rules for changing a choice | `buildPicker`, `choose`, `pickerReady` in `src/alloykit/picker.ts` |
+| Saved choice and the connection check | `saveSelection`, `connectAlloy` in `src/alloyhost/choice.ts` |
+| Reading the saved choice | `readSavedSelection` in `src/alloyhost/savedSelection.ts`, used by `src/alloyhost/appRouter.ts` |
+
+For the Shopify sign-in and location, see [[settings/shopify]].
